---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import DatabaseCard from '../components/DatabaseCard.astro';
import { databases } from '../data/db';
import { publicOvdbApiCount, storageEntryCount, storageGroups } from '../data/ovdb';
const totalTables = databases.reduce((sum, db) => sum + db.tables.filter((table) => table.kind === 'table').length, 0);
const totalViews = databases.reduce((sum, db) => sum + db.tables.filter((table) => table.kind === 'view').length, 0);
---
<SiteLayout title="DemoDB — Sample databases for developers" description="Explore open sample databases with reliable downloads, schema references, and machine-readable metadata.">
  <section class="hero shell catalogue-hero">
    <div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span>Sample data, ready to use</p><h1>Good data makes<br /><em>better examples.</em></h1><p class="hero-lede">A dependable home for the sample databases developers use to learn, test, and build. Browse the schema, preview records, and download a fixture in the format you need.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#databases">Explore databases <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="button button-quiet" href="/ovdb/">Explore OpenVaultDB server <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button button-quiet" href="https://github.com/demo-db">Open data contracts ↗</a></div></div>
    <div class="hero-console" aria-label="DemoDB catalogue summary"><div class="console-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><code>demodb.dev</code></div><div class="console-content"><p class="console-comment">-- curated sample databases</p><p><span class="syntax-key">SELECT</span> schema, records</p><p><span class="syntax-key">FROM</span> trusted_fixtures <span class="syntax-key">WHERE</span> useful = true;</p><div class="console-rule"></div><p class="console-result">{databases.map((db) => db.name).join('  ·  ')}</p><p class="console-comment">-- {databases.length} databases · {totalTables} tables · {totalViews} views</p></div></div>
  </section>
  <section id="databases" class="shell section intro-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">The collection</p><h2>Familiar data.<br />Clear provenance.</h2></div><div class="intro-copy"><p>Each database has its own source repository and reproducible contract. DemoDB combines those contracts into one catalogue while keeping the schema, licensing, and downloadable files close to their owners.</p><p>Start with a music shop or a small business, then follow the relationships through real tables and sample queries.</p></div></section>
  <section class="shell section"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Browse sample databases</p><h2>Choose a dataset to explore.</h2></div><span class="muted">{databases.length} registered databases</span></div><div class="database-grid">{databases.map((db) => <DatabaseCard db={db} />)}</div></section>
  <section class="shell section ovdb-home-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">OpenVaultDB server</p><h2>Explore the same data<br /><em>through a read-only API.</em></h2><p>Browse six published SQLite databases through OpenVaultDB, plus hosted PostgreSQL, Git-hosted inGitDB, and authenticated-reader BigQuery editions. BigQuery query jobs use your own selected execution project.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/ovdb/">Browse server and storage catalogue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="ovdb-home-facts"><div><strong>{storageGroups.length}</strong><span>datasets</span></div><div><strong>{storageEntryCount}</strong><span>storage entries</span></div><div><strong>{publicOvdbApiCount}</strong><span>public OVDB APIs</span></div></div></section>
  <section class="shell section catalogue-note"><p class="eyebrow">For builders</p><h2>Stable files. Reusable contracts.</h2><p>Download SQLite, SQL, CSV, and JSON exports where available. Machine-readable schema contracts keep column types, keys, relationships, and row counts aligned with each fixture.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/demo-db/websites">Read how the catalogue is built →</a></section>
</SiteLayout>
